  "note": "(anim-skeleton S3b; A8; keyed by hand, never traced; studio only, never played by the game) The skeleton test: the clavicle, finger and FK leg channels together, standing on the spot (48 frames, 2 s in the studio). f0-10 both shoulders shrug 20 deg (clav roll +20, f5); f10-19 the right shoulder pushed forward 25 deg (clav yaw -25, f14-16); f12-24 the fingers curl one at a time (index, middle, ring, little, thumb; curl +0.85, the thumb +0.8, on top of the relaxed hand), a fist to f27, then open (curl a little below the relaxed hand) and spread (thumb 20, index 12, ring 10, little 18 deg) at f31-34, relaxed by f36; f24-48 a left-leg FK kick: the FK weight w 0 -> 1 (f24-28), chamber f31 (hip flex 60, knee 70, ankle -20 = plantarflexed, toe +20 = up), extension f36 (hip 70, knee 15), recoil f42 (hip 50, knee 70), w back to 0 by f48 with the leg at rest; the pelvis eases 2.5 cm over the standing right leg (w 0 throughout: the foot planner's leg). Arms otherwise relaxed, the trunk near neutral. Conventions as the other key files (degrees, body frame x right, y up, z forward), plus (scripts/anim-keys/py/key_clip.py): `clav` {pitch, yaw, roll} per arm in the chest frame, right side as written and the left mirrored (roll + lifts, yaw - pushes forward); `handL` / `handR` per finger {curl (1 = closed, added to the grip shape), spread (deg, + away from the middle finger)}; `legL` / `legR` `toe` (deg, + the toes up) and `w` (FK weight 0..1; keep 0 on frames where the foot is on the ground). `checkFrames`: the bake's frame proof (tests/fixtures/keyed-check-skeleton_test.json).",
